# Package template: copy this directory to packages/<group>/<name>/ and edit package.env.
#
# package.env is sourced by build() with PKG_TARGET, TOOLCHAIN, HARCH, HM, HOS, PLATFORM_NAME,
# INSTALL_*, GCC_VER and the other framework variables already set: it only assigns variables,
# nothing else runs from here and no case or if is needed. This file describes the default
# build; what differs for a build target, a toolchain, an architecture, a platform, a version
# or an option goes into a variant directory, applied on top of it when its selector matches:
#   variants/target/<native|cross|sysroot|default|name>/   the build target (":<target>")
#   variants/toolchain/<gnu|llvm>/                          the toolchain the package uses
#   variants/arch/<HM>/  variants/platform/<PLATFORM_NAME>/  variants/version/<PKG_VER>/
#   variants/option/<name>/ and variants/option/<name>=<value>/  WITH_<NAME> set by the project
# A name may list several values (target/native,cross) and the axes nest in that order for a
# conjunction (target/default/arch/arm). A variant replaces (=) or extends (+=) the values of
# this file: a target that must not have a default dependency restates PKG_DEPS. Every variant
# directory has this same layout: its package.env is sourced after this one, its scripts
# replace the ones below, its patches/ files join (or replace, by name) the ones of the recipe.
# The build steps live next to it as real scripts, written like any other Bash file:
#   prebuild.sh     runs in the source directory before autoreconf/configure (set -x, no -e)
#   build.sh        the whole build when BUILD_PROCESS=custom (bash -ex, in the build directory)
#   postbuild.sh    runs in the build directory after the build process (set -ex)
#   postinstall.sh  copied into the sysroot and sourced as root inside the target image
#   files/          static files, referenced as ${PKG_RECIPEPATH}/files/<name>
#   patches/        *.patch and *.diff files applied in name order (00-first.patch, 10-second.patch)
# Inside every script all the ALL_CAPS variables visible here are available as ${VAR}
# (INSTALL_PREFIX, PKG_PKGPATH, PKG_SRCPATH, HARCH, PKG_VARIANTS...) together with the toolchain
# environment (SYSROOT, CC, CFLAGS, PATH...). Editing any file of the directory rebuilds the package.
# Check the directory with utilities/pkg_lint packages/<group>/<name> and see what a build
# would get with utilities/pkg_show <group>/<name>[:<target>].

###### Package definition ######

### PKG_URL: (*) URL(s) of the sources, space separated
PKG_URL="http://packages.org/package-1.0.tar.gz"
### GIT_URL / GIT_COMMIT: clone a repository instead of downloading an archive
#GIT_URL="https://git.example.org/package.git"
#GIT_COMMIT="tags/v1.0"
### PKG_VER: version, appended to the package name (<name>_<PKG_VER>)
PKG_VER=1.0
### PKG_SUFFIX: extra suffix for the package name
#PKG_SUFFIX="-custom"
### PKG_SRCDIR: source directory name under sources/ (default: the package full name)
#PKG_SRCDIR="package-1.0"
### PKG_DEPS: dependencies built first, <group>/<name>[:native|:cross|:<target>]
PKG_DEPS="lfs/zlib lfs/bison:native"
### PKG_CHECK: probe that replaces the status file (mandatory for :native builds)
#PKG_CHECK="[ -f ${INSTALL_EXECPREFIX}/bin/package ]"

###### Prebuild process ######

### PATCHDEB: Debian source package whose debian/patches/series is applied
#PATCHDEB="http://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/p/package/package_1.0-1.debian.tar.xz"
### The patches of the package are the files of patches/ (see patches/README.md), no variable
### PKG_AUTOCONF: run autoreconf -fi before configure (default 0)
#PKG_AUTOCONF=1
### AUTOCONF_PATH: subdirectory where autoreconf runs
#AUTOCONF_PATH=subdir

###### Build process ######

### BUILD_PROCESS: (*) one of
###   downloadonly configmake cmakebuild mesonninja cargobuild simplemake pythonbuild
###   perlmodule kernelbuild kernelmodbuild custom none
BUILD_PROCESS=configmake
### PKG_COPYSRC: copy the sources into the build directory (default 0 for configmake, 1 otherwise)
#PKG_COPYSRC=1
### CONF_CMD / CONF_PATH: configure command and subdirectory where the build runs
#CONF_CMD="configure_new"
#CONF_PATH=subdir
### CONF_FLAGS / CONF_VARS / CONF_ENV: configure, cmake or meson arguments, trailing VAR=value
### assignments and command prefix. References such as '${SYSROOT}' are expanded when the
### generated runconfig.sh runs, so single quotes are enough for the build environment values.
CONF_FLAGS="--disable-feature"
#CONF_VARS="ac_cv_something=yes"
#CONF_ENV="env -u CPP"
### PKG_CFLAGS / PKG_CXXFLAGS / PKG_LDFLAGS: extra compiler and linker flags
#PKG_CFLAGS="-Wno-error"
### PKG_MAKEENV / PKG_MAKEVARS / PKG_MAKETARGETS: make prefix, variables and comma separated targets
#PKG_MAKEVARS="V=1"
PKG_MAKETARGETS="all,install-strip"
### PKG_OVERRIDELTO / PKG_OVERRIDELD / PKG_OVERRIDESHARED / PKG_OVERRIDESTATIC: per package overrides
#PKG_OVERRIDELTO=0
### PKG_TOOLCHAIN: force gnu or llvm for this package
#PKG_TOOLCHAIN=gnu

### Options: give WITH_<NAME> a default here and put what it adds in variants/option/<name>/
### (see variants/option/docs/): the project overrides it with WITH_DOCS=0
WITH_DOCS=${WITH_DOCS:-1}

###### Post install ######

### PKG_POSTINSTALL_PRIO: order of postinstall.sh among the post install scripts (default 50)
#PKG_POSTINSTALL_PRIO=50
